# Fixed-width initializer rejects an overflowed element expression

Verifies an `int8[]` initializer refuses a value the declared width cannot
hold even though evaluating `127 + 1` promoted the result to `int16`. The
destination representation contract applies to the final value, not to the
temporary width used while the expression was evaluated.

>>> source
let a: int8[] = [127 + 1]
print(a[0])

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: array element `128` cannot be represented as `int8`

<<< exit
1
